    "guide": [
      [
        "Match airflow to your room",
        "<p>CADR is clean air delivered per hour. A common rule of thumb is to choose a CADR of at least about five times your room volume in cubic metres, which our room size tool applies. A 5 by 4 metre room with a 2.6 metre ceiling needs roughly 260 m3/h. Brand coverage claims use different test rules, so treat them as indicators.</p>"
      ],
      [
        "Filters and running costs",
        "<p>HEPA filters trap fine particles but need replacing, from about every year for Prism+ and Acerpure to up to two years for Sharp and Panasonic models, as ProductNation reports. Budget for filters and electricity, from about 20 W for the Blueair to 72 W for the LG.</p>"
      ],
      [
        "Noise, sensors and what is overhyped",
        "<p>Sleep modes at 18 to 30 dB suit bedrooms. Sensors help automatic modes but do not prove better cleaning. Ionizers and nanoe-style features are brand technologies whose benefits we could not verify independently, so we did not give them weight.</p>"
      ],
      [
        "Placement and everyday use",
        "<p>Place the purifier a little away from walls so air can flow in and out, keep doors and windows closed while it runs, and run it on the highest setting when the haze is heavy or you are cooking. Vacuum the pre-filter every few weeks if the manual allows. A purifier cannot remove gases such as cooking fumes unless it has a carbon or equivalent filter, which varies by model.</p>"
      ]
    ],
    "faq": [
      [
        "Do air purifiers work for haze in Malaysia?",
        "HEPA filters capture fine particles, which is the main concern in haze, but results depend on room size and airflow. Keep windows closed and pick CADR that suits the room."
      ],
      [
        "Is a cheap purifier like the Xiaomi 4 Compact enough?",
        "For a small bedroom, yes in principle. ProductNation warns it is too small for open-plan areas, and its CADR figures conflict across pages."
      ],
      [
        "How often should I replace filters?",
        "Vendors claim from about one to two years, depending on model and usage. Replace sooner in dusty or haze-heavy conditions and follow the manual."
      ],
      [
        "Is a Dyson worth it?",
        "It adds formaldehyde sensing and a fan, with strong brand support. If you only need particle filtering, cheaper options may do the job."
      ]
    ]
